        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set deconstructs the user's broad interest in \"workflow\" and \"flow state\" into distinct, research-worthy avenues. The topics move beyond simple \"how-to\" guides and instead frame workflow as a design problem rooted in cognitive psychology, systems thinking, and behavioral science. They are designed to explore the \"why\" and \"how\" behind effective systems: how workflows induce flow, how they are measured, how tools shape them, and why they \"feel right.\" These topics provide a foundation for understanding and implementing a high-level personal development project.",
