      "unordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Context Switching Costs:** A deep dive into the specific cognitive penalties (time, energy, and error rate) associated with moving between different tasks, projects, or tools.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 123,
          "source": "topic-set_workflow-design-and-cognitive-optimization_🆔20251028231740.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Decision Fatigue:** The psychological concept that the quality of one's decisions deteriorates after a long session of decision-making, and how workflow design can mitigate this.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 123,
          "source": "topic-set_workflow-design-and-cognitive-optimization_🆔20251028231740.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Attentional Residue:** The phenomenon where thoughts about a *previous* task linger and interfere with your focus on the *current* task, and how \"shutdown routines\" can combat it.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 130,
          "source": "topic-set_workflow-design-and-cognitive-optimization_🆔20251028231740.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Systems Thinking vs. Linear Thinking:** An exploration of how viewing your work as an interconnected *system* (with inputs, outputs, and feedback loops) rather than a linear \"to-do list\" can unlock new levels of efficiency.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 130,
          "source": "topic-set_workflow-design-and-cognitive-optimization_🆔20251028231740.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Human-Computer Interaction (HCI):** The academic field that studies the design and use of computer technology, focusing on the interfaces between users and computers. This is the formal discipline behind \"why a workflow feels right.\"",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 141,
          "source": "topic-set_workflow-design-and-cognitive-optimization_🆔20251028231740.md"
        }
      ]
